# apps.rst, wake_latency (M2): wrapped ISR, k_sem (the default).
# Schematic: 1 unit is 1 pixel; the box widths fit the labels, they are
# not durations. The masks are those of the pinned trees (both the same).
include apps.tdc
diagram wake-latency "wake_latency, wrapped-sem: the ISR wakes a thread, three histograms"
schematic
axis "time after the edge (schematic)" -30..791

waker pending -30.. "blocked in k_sem_take()"
@edge
hw 76 "pin, NVIC" : Edge, EXTI, NVIC. The pending interrupt wakes the core.
@pending anchor
idle sleep -30..pending "WFI" {primask} : The idle thread sleeps in WFI with PRIMASK set.
idle 49 "cpsie" {primask} : The idle thread clears PRIMASK. Only then can the interrupt start.
hw 49 "entry" : Exception entry.
dev 60 "wrapper" : _isr_wrapper. With LATBENCH_WAKE_ISR_DIRECT, this step is not there.
dev 36 "now" : The first action of the ISR: t_isr = stim_now().
@t_isr
dev 43 "give" {basepri} : k_sem_give() makes the woken thread ready. It holds the semaphore spinlock (BASEPRI) for the whole call. In an ISR, it does not switch.
dev 43 "exit" : The ISR exit pends PendSV, because the ready thread is not the current thread.
pendsv 56 "switch" {basepri 16..40} : PendSV saves the registers of the idle thread. With BASEPRI, it takes the woken thread from the ready queue cache. Then it restores the BASEPRI of the woken thread (0) and its registers.
waker 36 "now" : The first action after k_sem_take() returns: t_thr = stim_now().
@t_thr
waker 43 "hist" : irq, isr2thr and irq2thr, and the two phase histograms.
waker 82 "stim_arm()" {basepri} : Programs the next edge, with irq_lock() (BASEPRI).
waker 43 "take" {basepri} : k_sem_take() blocks again. It holds BASEPRI from k_spin_lock() until arch_swap() pends PendSV and unlocks.
@waker_blocks anchor
waker pending waker_blocks..791 "blocked"
pendsv 56 "switch" {basepri 16..40} : PendSV switches back to the idle thread.
idle 49 "idle" {basepri} : The idle loop: arch_irq_lock() sets BASEPRI. Then k_cpu_idle() sets PRIMASK and clears BASEPRI.
@sleeps anchor
idle sleep sleeps..791 "WFI" {primask}
span edge..t_isr "irq" !
span t_isr..t_thr "isr2thr" !
span edge..t_thr "irq2thr" !
